# No leftover temp files after features

## Mandate

Finish a WZ/MCP/GUI feature → **remove** temporary process files from the orange-wz tree. Do not leave verify dumps, MCP run logs, or one-off probe Java at the repo root.

## Delete (examples)

- Logs: `*.log`, `*.err`, `mcp-*.log`, `mcp_*.log`, `orange-wz-*.log`, `convert_full.log`, `merge_full*.log`
- WZ scratch at repo root: `0243_*.img`, `*_verify.img.xml`, `Consume_*.img*`, `String_Consume_*`, `_tmp*`
- One-off probes: `Verify*.java`, `Dump*.java`, `Diagnose*.java`, `tools/*.class`

## Keep

- Production sources under `src/main/java`
- Intentional long-lived tools already tracked under `tools/` (not underscore scratch)

## Git

Rely on `.gitignore` patterns above so junk is not re-added. Never force-push; never commit `mcp-runtime/` licensed blobs.
